  "details": "As told to me in discord, the interact Outline goes by mesh renderer ON the script object, then any child mesh renderer, and if none of them, it uses the collider.\n\nWhy should it check the children when the script object already has a collider? Especially when the child mesh renderer is small.\n\nI'll even settle for an udonbehaviour bool \"ForceInteractOutlineCollider\" where it forces the outline to use a collider.",
